2026-05-26 14:08:05,817 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with EuroCloud Solutions S.A. and GreenCompute S.r.l., proposes an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in their daily administrative tasks. Our solution leverages cutting-edge technologies, including the Mistral 7B Instruct model for language understanding, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) for information retrieval, and a microservices-based architecture for scalability and reliability.

# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval requires an AI-powered solution that can assist municipal agents in accessing reliable and up-to-date information, drafting administrative contents, instructing files, and collaborating with other services. The solution must comply with regulatory requirements, including GDPR, and ensure a high level of security and explicability.

# Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution integrates the following components:
1. **Technical Architecture**: We will design a microservices-based system using containerization (Docker) and orchestration (Kubernetes). This architecture will facilitate flexible scalability, meeting the availability requirement of 99.9%. For integration with existing systems, we will utilize API standards such as REST, GraphQL, and SOAP, along with API gateways like Kong and Apigee.
2. **AI Components**: We will employ the Mistral 7B Instruct model for language understanding, fine-tuned using our LoRA or QLoRA methods on a domain-specific corpus. Our RAG capabilities will be utilized to facilitate access to information by integrating with existing practices of agents. For explainability, we will implement xAI methods such as source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, and LIME.
3. **Security and Compliance**: We hold ISO 27001 certification, which includes the scope of design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems. Our data residency is EU-only, and we have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed. For anonymization, we use Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models.
4. **Budget and Cost Optimization**: Our target gross margin percentage is 28%. Given the global budget of 3 million euros over 4 years, our projected revenue from this contract would be 3 million euros, with a required cost of approximately 2,160,000 euros to achieve our target gross margin. We propose cost optimization strategies such as rate renegotiation with subcontractors and scope reduction.
5. **Sustainability**: Our solution will utilize green hosting partners like OVHcloud or Scaleway, both of which use 100% renewable energy. We aim for an average energy reduction of about 35% compared to our baseline.

# Unaddressed Requirements
None of the requirements specified by the City of Belval are left unaddressed in this proposal.

# Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with EuroCloud Solutions S.A. and GreenCompute S.r.l., is confident that our proposed solution meets all the requirements specified by the City of Belval. Our team has the necessary expertise, experience, and capabilities to deliver a high-quality AI-powered solution that assists municipal agents in their administrative tasks while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and minimizing environmental footprint. We look forward to the opportunity to discuss this proposal in further detail.
